title: milo_onboarding
tags: moon1 onboarding tutorial
position: 0,0
---
Milo: Hey — traveler. Easy now. The mud here doesn't bite, but the silence does. [voice:milo_onboarding_01]
Milo: Name's Milo. Mapmaker, mostly. Occasionally a thief, when the map demands it. [voice:milo_onboarding_02]
Milo: This is Echohaven. Or what's left of it. Buried, hushed, waiting. [voice:milo_onboarding_03]
Milo: Three buildings still have a pulse under the muck. Three. That's it. [voice:milo_onboarding_04]
Milo: The Fountain to the west — it remembers water. The Dome south of here — it remembers light. The Spire to the north — it remembers song. [voice:milo_onboarding_05]
Milo: Restore them and the town wakes up. Fail and we leave it sleeping. Your call. [voice:milo_onboarding_06]
Milo: Start with the Fountain. See that beacon? Pale ring of dust, faint hum on the air. That's it. [voice:milo_onboarding_07]
Milo: Walk to the tuning pedestal beside it. Hold E. Slide the dial until the stone agrees with you. [voice:milo_onboarding_08]
Milo: Don't rush. The frequency knows when you're guessing. [voice:milo_onboarding_09]
Milo: When it lands, you'll feel it in your teeth. Then the mud lets go and the building remembers what it was. [voice:milo_onboarding_10]
Milo: I'll keep my distance. I'm useful, not pretty. Holler if anything tries to eat you. [voice:milo_onboarding_11]
Milo: Three buildings, traveler. Then we talk about what comes next. [voice:milo_onboarding_12]
===
